#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""Direct causal state-action policy research for four liquid crypto perpetuals.

This candidate deliberately does not begin with hand-authored trade plans.  It
observes a dense, causal market state at regular decision times, enumerates a
small set of economically distinct stop/target geometries, learns their
cost-after action value, and lets one account choose at most one action across
BTCUSDT, ETHUSDT, SOLUSDT and XRPUSDT.

The fast research simulator is intentionally independent from order/accounting
plumbing.  A policy with durable evidence is meant to be moved into the existing
NautilusTrader continuous-account runner for canonical execution validation.
"""
